  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Exoplanet Transit Classification\n",
        "\n",
        "**Machine learning experiments on Kepler light-curve data**\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook investigates how different model architectures classify stars as having a detected exoplanet or not. It compares a multilayer perceptron (MLP), a fully connected neural network, and a one-dimensional convolutional neural network (1D CNN)."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "pPu6lFdWemiG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "m0ygrZd3dmu5"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Project overview\n",
        "\n",
        "The goal is to evaluate several machine-learning approaches for binary exoplanet classification using the provided Kepler-derived light-curve dataset. The workflow includes signal preprocessing, training-set class balancing, model training, and evaluation on a held-out test set.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Models\n",
        "- **MLP:** a scikit-learn baseline with one hidden layer.\n",
        "- **Dense neural network:** a Keras feed-forward model.\n",
        "- **1D CNN:** a convolutional model designed to learn local patterns across the ordered signal features.\n",
        "\n",
        "The models are evaluated using test accuracy and confusion matrices. Because exoplanet-positive examples are rare, accuracy should be interpreted alongside the confusion matrices and class-specific metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "irPDgkzsdguU"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 1. Data and approach\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset contains measurements represented as ordered light-curve features and a binary label. The original labels are converted from `1`/`2` to `0`/`1`, where `1` represents the positive exoplanet class after conversion.\n",
        "\n",
        "The notebook uses the supplied training and test files. The test set remains separate from resampling: preprocessing transformations are fitted on training data and then applied to test data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Runtime note\n",
        "\n",
        "Training neural networks is faster with a GPU. In Google Colab, select **Runtime → Change runtime type → T4 GPU** if one is available. CPU execution may take longer."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Gd53z1-PfLTx"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PjzYKqcweS2F",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "f25e2d1c-8b05-4a9f-e697-28893390618f"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Download the dataset files when they are not already present.\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "import urllib.request\n",
        "\n",
        "DATA_URL = (\n",
        "    \"https://storage.googleapis.com/inspirit-ai-data-bucket-1/Data/\"\n",
        "    \"AI%20Scholars/Sessions%206%20-%2010%20(Projects)/Project%20-%20Planet%20Hunters/\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "for filename in (\"exoTrain.csv\", \"exoTest.csv\"):\n",
        "    if not Path(filename).exists():\n",
        "        urllib.request.urlretrieve(DATA_URL + filename, filename)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Core data and visualization libraries\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "# Preprocessing and evaluation\n",
        "from scipy.signal import savgol_filter\n",
        "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n",
        "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
        "    accuracy_score,\n",
        "    classification_report,\n",
        "    confusion_matrix,\n",
        "    ConfusionMatrixDisplay,\n",
        ")\n",
        "from sklearn.neural_network import MLPClassifier\n",
        "from sklearn.preprocessing import RobustScaler, normalize\n",
        "\n",
        "# Neural-network libraries\n",
        "import tensorflow as tf\n",
        "from keras.layers import Dense, Conv1D, MaxPooling1D, Flatten\n",
        "from keras.models import Sequential\n",
        "\n",
        "# Load data and convert labels from 1/2 to 0/1.\n",
        "df_train = pd.read_csv(\"exoTrain.csv\")\n",
        "df_test = pd.read_csv(\"exoTest.csv\")\n",
        "df_train[\"LABEL\"] = df_train[\"LABEL\"] - 1\n",
        "df_test[\"LABEL\"] = df_test[\"LABEL\"] - 1\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train = df_train.drop(columns=\"LABEL\")\n",
        "y_train = df_train[\"LABEL\"]\n",
        "X_test = df_test.drop(columns=\"LABEL\")\n",
        "y_test = df_test[\"LABEL\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_training_history(history, evaluation):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Plot training and validation accuracy and loss.\"\"\"\n",
        "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4))\n",
        "\n",
        "    axes[0].plot(history.history[\"accuracy\"], label=\"Training\")\n",
        "    axes[0].plot(history.history[\"val_accuracy\"], label=\"Validation\")\n",
        "    axes[0].set(title=f\"Accuracy (final test accuracy: {evaluation[1]:.3f})\",\n",
        "                xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"Accuracy\")\n",
        "    axes[0].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "    axes[1].plot(history.history[\"loss\"], label=\"Training\")\n",
        "    axes[1].plot(history.history[\"val_loss\"], label=\"Validation\")\n",
        "    axes[1].set(title=f\"Loss (test loss: {evaluation[0]:.3f})\",\n",
        "                xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"Loss\")\n",
        "    axes[1].legend()\n",
        "\n",
        "    fig.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.show()\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def analyze_results(model, X_train, y_train, X_test, y_test):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Display confusion matrices for training and test data.\"\"\"\n",
        "    is_keras_model = isinstance(model, Sequential)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def predict_labels(features):\n",
        "        if is_keras_model:\n",
        "            return (model.predict(features, verbose=0).ravel() >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
        "        return model.predict(features)\n",
        "\n",
        "    for split_name, features, labels in (\n",
        "        (\"Training\", X_train, y_train),\n",
        "        (\"Test\", X_test, y_test),\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        predictions = predict_labels(features)\n",
        "        matrix = confusion_matrix(labels, predictions, labels=[0, 1])\n",
        "\n",
        "        plt.figure(figsize=(5, 4))\n",
        "        sns.heatmap(\n",
        "            matrix,\n",
        "            annot=True,\n",
        "            fmt=\"d\",\n",
        "            cmap=\"Blues\",\n",
        "            xticklabels=[\"Non-exoplanet\", \"Exoplanet\"],\n",
        "            yticklabels=[\"Non-exoplanet\", \"Exoplanet\"],\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        plt.title(f\"{split_name} confusion matrix\")\n",
        "        plt.xlabel(\"Predicted label\")\n",
        "        plt.ylabel(\"True label\")\n",
        "        plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "        plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "        if split_name == \"Test\":\n",
        "            print(classification_report(\n",
        "                labels, predictions,\n",
        "                target_names=[\"Non-exoplanet\", \"Exoplanet\"],\n",
        "                zero_division=0,\n",
        "            ))\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a-xGYMhu8tu7"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PAc67kxQftEV"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 2. Preprocessing\n",
        "\n",
        "The training and test data are loaded into separate feature matrices and label vectors. The preprocessing pipeline applies a Fourier transform, Savitzky–Golay filtering, row normalization, and robust scaling. SMOTE is then applied **only to the training data** to address class imbalance.\n",
        "\n",
        "These transformations are retained as experimental choices for this project; their impact should be assessed by comparing results against simpler preprocessing baselines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6yRtFD1pYP7d"
      },
      "source": [
        "def apply_smote(features, labels):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Balance the training classes with SMOTE.\"\"\"\n",
        "    sampler = SMOTE(random_state=1)\n",
        "    return sampler.fit_resample(features, labels)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def apply_savgol(train_features, test_features):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Smooth each feature sequence with a Savitzky–Golay filter.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return (\n",
        "        savgol_filter(train_features, 21, 4, axis=1),\n",
        "        savgol_filter(test_features, 21, 4, axis=1),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def apply_fourier(train_features, test_features):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Return the magnitude of the Fourier transform for each sample.\"\"\"\n",
        "    return (\n",
        "        np.abs(np.fft.fft(train_features, axis=1)),\n",
        "        np.abs(np.fft.fft(test_features, axis=1)),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def apply_normalization(train_features, test_features):\n",
        "    return normalize(train_features), normalize(test_features)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def apply_robust_scaling(train_features, test_features):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Fit the scaler on training data and apply it to both splits.\"\"\"\n",
        "    scaler = RobustScaler()\n",
        "    return (\n",
        "        scaler.fit_transform(train_features),\n",
        "        scaler.transform(test_features),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "fourier_X_train, fourier_X_test = apply_fourier(X_train, X_test)\n",
        "savgol_X_train, savgol_X_test = apply_savgol(fourier_X_train, fourier_X_test)\n",
        "norm_X_train, norm_X_test = apply_normalization(savgol_X_train, savgol_X_test)\n",
        "robust_X_train, robust_X_test = apply_robust_scaling(norm_X_train, norm_X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Resample only the training split.\n",
        "smote_X_train, smote_y_train = apply_smote(robust_X_train, y_train)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mRQPCRgpZVpW"
      },
      "source": [
        "The processed variables used below are:\n",
        "\n",
        "- `smote_X_train`, `smote_y_train`: preprocessed and resampled training data.\n",
        "- `robust_X_test`, `y_test`: preprocessed, unresampled test data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Keeping the test set unresampled preserves the original class distribution for evaluation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sw7FwS0_W7Bx"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Model A — Multilayer perceptron\n",
        "\n",
        "The first model is a scikit-learn `MLPClassifier` with one hidden layer of 10 units. It provides a compact neural-network baseline for comparison with the Keras models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dmbSCBCH2I9p"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Model configuration\n",
        "\n",
        "The model uses a fixed random seed for reproducibility and a maximum of 300 training iterations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9rVs2i_C_F1o"
      },
      "source": [
        "# MLP baseline: one hidden layer with 10 units.\n",
        "model = MLPClassifier(\n",
        "    hidden_layer_sizes=(10,),\n",
        "    random_state=1,\n",
        "    max_iter=300,\n",
        ")\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WXj7fzfkXuQ9"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Train and evaluate\n",
        "\n",
        "Fit the MLP on the resampled training set, then evaluate it on the untouched test set. The training score is included as a diagnostic; the test score is the more relevant estimate of generalization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5okHo29ZXt13",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 1000
        },
        "outputId": "af3e996b-ecc1-4457-871c-16571644e7e4"
      },
      "source": [
        "model.fit(smote_X_train, smote_y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "train_predictions = model.predict(smote_X_train)\n",
        "test_predictions = model.predict(robust_X_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training accuracy: {accuracy_score(smote_y_train, train_predictions):.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test accuracy:     {accuracy_score(y_test, test_predictions):.4f}\")\n",
        "analyze_results(model, smote_X_train, smote_y_train, robust_X_test, y_test)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "UdW3vidfZQxg"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Interpretation\n",
        "\n",
        "Review the test accuracy and confusion matrix. In particular, consider how many positive examples are detected and how many are missed. A high overall accuracy can be misleading when the positive class is rare."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "9cYzv7-ZvNMb"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Further experiment: MLP\n",
        "\n",
        "To extend this experiment, vary the number of hidden layers and units, and compare results using the same test set. You can also compare the processed features with the original features. Record the configuration and metrics for each run so the comparisons remain reproducible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TRF34weGoClK"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 4. Model B — Fully connected neural network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qbCq5LpQgVkF"
      },
      "source": [
        "This model uses Keras to build a feed-forward neural network with a ReLU hidden layer and a sigmoid output. The sigmoid output produces a probability-like score for the positive class, making binary cross-entropy an appropriate loss function."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "shZOUCAbBJ0M"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Fully connected neural network.\n",
        "model = Sequential([\n",
        "    Dense(10, activation=\"relu\", input_shape=(X_train.shape[1],)),\n",
        "    Dense(1, activation=\"sigmoid\"),\n",
        "])\n",
        "model.compile(\n",
        "    loss=\"binary_crossentropy\",\n",
        "    optimizer=\"adam\",\n",
        "    metrics=[\"accuracy\"],\n",
        ")\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "sriqCvylFPSE"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Architecture summary\n",
        "\n",
        "Inspect the model summary to confirm the input dimensions and the number of trainable parameters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gUdk-_M3FTqA",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "0271569c-f024-40d9-c139-2145d421c29d"
      },
      "source": [
        "model.summary()"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6QaGfpePBSKS"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Train the network\n",
        "\n",
        "The network is trained for up to 20 epochs with batches of 64 samples. The held-out test set is supplied as validation data so that loss and accuracy can be monitored during training. For a more rigorous final evaluation, avoid using test-set results to repeatedly tune model choices."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b9Y1kOWtnOTv",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "outputId": "95a10211-2c9b-4d78-e023-b06579dc4300"
      },
      "source": [
        "history = model.fit(\n",
        "    smote_X_train,\n",
        "    smote_y_train,\n",
        "    batch_size=64,\n",
        "    epochs=20,\n",
        "    verbose=1,\n",
        "    validation_data=(robust_X_test, y_test),\n",
        "    shuffle=True,\n",
        ")\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "gIBRY5RnbrMY"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Training history and evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "The plots show training and validation accuracy and loss across epochs. The confusion matrices provide a complementary view of class-specific errors."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "VDly6NJObeiP",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 1000
        },
        "outputId": "d12e0850-a916-4611-8a6a-beb0df0b7c1c"
      },
      "source": [
        "test_performance = model.evaluate(robust_X_test, y_test, batch_size=64, verbose=0)\n",
        "print(f\"Test loss: {test_performance[0]:.4f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Test accuracy: {test_performance[1]:.4f}\")\n",
        "plot_training_history(history, test_performance)\n",
        "analyze_results(model, smote_X_train, smote_y_train, robust_X_test, y_test)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "YbrQWbPYhfwZ"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Further experiment: dense network\n",
        "\n",
        "Try changing the number of hidden layers or units. Compare the resulting test metrics with the baseline while keeping the preprocessing and evaluation procedure consistent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BlXvkwTEhpNw"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Use this cell for a documented dense-network experiment.\n",
        "# Example: change the hidden-layer width, retrain, and record test metrics.\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MA_rRs1jTjDw"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 5. Model C — One-dimensional convolutional neural network\n",
        "\n",
        "A fully connected network can be sensitive to where patterns appear in an input sequence. A 1D CNN applies learned filters across adjacent features, allowing it to detect local patterns at different positions. This experiment reshapes each sample to `(number_of_features, 1)` so it can be processed by `Conv1D` layers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NnQlAZ043qOo"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Prepare the CNN inputs\n",
        "\n",
        "The reshape operation changes the array dimensions without changing the underlying values. Both the resampled training features and the preprocessed test features are reshaped for the CNN. The original, unprocessed features are also reshaped for optional comparisons."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ZMWiJnl735CQ"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Reshape each sample to (features, channels) for Conv1D.\n",
        "cnn_smote_X_train = np.expand_dims(smote_X_train, axis=-1)\n",
        "cnn_smote_y_train = np.asarray(smote_y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "cnn_preprocess_X_test = np.expand_dims(robust_X_test, axis=-1)\n",
        "cnn_preprocess_y_test = np.asarray(y_test)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Original features, reshaped for optional baseline comparisons.\n",
        "cnn_X_train = np.expand_dims(X_train.to_numpy(), axis=-1)\n",
        "cnn_y_train = np.asarray(y_train)\n",
        "cnn_X_test = np.expand_dims(X_test.to_numpy(), axis=-1)\n",
        "cnn_y_test = np.asarray(y_test)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "rtHMC1fJWsrM"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Verify input dimensions\n",
        "\n",
        "The expected feature-array shape is `(samples, features, 1)`, while the label arrays remain one-dimensional."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Fcti4YgIXdN4"
      },
      "source": [
        "print(\"Resampled training features:\", cnn_smote_X_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Training labels:\", cnn_smote_y_train.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Preprocessed test features:\", cnn_preprocess_X_test.shape)\n",
        "print(\"Test labels:\", cnn_preprocess_y_test.shape)\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fW5bXRoaCTIj"
      },
      "source": [
        "### CNN architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "The network uses two convolutional layers, each followed by max pooling, then a flattening layer and a sigmoid output. The architecture is intentionally compact to provide a baseline for experiments with deeper networks, different filter counts, or dropout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dmW5k1otDu79"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Compact one-dimensional CNN.\n",
        "model = Sequential([\n",
        "    Conv1D(8, kernel_size=5, activation=\"relu\", padding=\"same\",\n",
        "           input_shape=(X_train.shape[1], 1)),\n",
        "    MaxPooling1D(pool_size=4, strides=4, padding=\"same\"),\n",
        "    Conv1D(16, kernel_size=3, activation=\"relu\", padding=\"same\"),\n",
        "    MaxPooling1D(pool_size=4, strides=4, padding=\"same\"),\n",
        "    Flatten(),\n",
        "    Dense(1, activation=\"sigmoid\"),\n",
        "])\n",
        "model.compile(\n",
        "    loss=\"binary_crossentropy\",\n",
        "    optimizer=\"adam\",\n",
        "    metrics=[\"accuracy\"],\n",
        ")\n"
      ],
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WbDT84eyDGHY"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Train the CNN\n",
        "\n",
        "Train using the reshaped, resampled training set and monitor performance on the preprocessed test set."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fqX49x9pDvql",
        "colab": {
